COMMENT ON TRIGGER preserve_history ON kodiak.audit_logs IS 'What: BEFORE UPDATE/DELETE trigger on audit_logs, tracking_events, booking_reviews, shipper_reviews and shipper_consignee_history. Why: Prevents accidental overwriting or deletion of historical evidence. How: Calls reject_history_mutation; ordinary application workflows append records instead.';
COMMENT ON TRIGGER preserve_history ON kodiak.tracking_events IS 'What: BEFORE UPDATE/DELETE trigger on audit_logs, tracking_events, booking_reviews, shipper_reviews and shipper_consignee_history. Why: Prevents accidental overwriting or deletion of historical evidence. How: Calls reject_history_mutation; ordinary application workflows append records instead.';
COMMENT ON TRIGGER preserve_history ON kodiak.booking_reviews IS 'What: BEFORE UPDATE/DELETE trigger on audit_logs, tracking_events, booking_reviews, shipper_reviews and shipper_consignee_history. Why: Prevents accidental overwriting or deletion of historical evidence. How: Calls reject_history_mutation; ordinary application workflows append records instead.';
COMMENT ON TRIGGER preserve_history ON kodiak.shipper_reviews IS 'What: BEFORE UPDATE/DELETE trigger on audit_logs, tracking_events, booking_reviews, shipper_reviews and shipper_consignee_history. Why: Prevents accidental overwriting or deletion of historical evidence. How: Calls reject_history_mutation; ordinary application workflows append records instead.';
COMMENT ON TRIGGER preserve_history ON kodiak.shipper_consignee_history IS 'What: BEFORE UPDATE/DELETE trigger on audit_logs, tracking_events, booking_reviews, shipper_reviews and shipper_consignee_history. Why: Prevents accidental overwriting or deletion of historical evidence. How: Calls reject_history_mutation; ordinary application workflows append records instead.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ux_users_email IS 'What: Unique index on normalized email. Why: Prevents duplicate logins differing only by case or surrounding spaces. How: Normalize email comparisons with lower(btrim(email)); duplicate writes fail.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ux_container_active_journey IS 'What: Unique partial index on allocated containers in open journeys. Why: Prevents concurrent double allocation. How: Applies only while endedon is null and containerid is set; closed movements do not prevent reuse.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ux_shipper_blacklist IS 'What: Unique partial index on shipper targets of open blacklists. Why: Prevents duplicate active restrictions for one shipper. How: Rows with null releasedon participate; released history permits a later new restriction.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ux_container_blacklist IS 'What: Unique partial index on container targets of open blacklists. Why: Prevents duplicate active restrictions for one container. How: Rows with null releasedon participate; released history remains available.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_shippers_consignee IS 'What: Index on current shipper consignee. Why: Supports listing the consignee''s current shipper network. How: Filter shippers by consigneeid; historical booking access uses booking assignment instead.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_bookings_shipper IS 'What: Index on shipper and descending creation time. Why: Supports recent booking lists for a shipper. How: Filter by shipperid and order by createdon descending.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_bookings_consignee IS 'What: Index on retained consignee and descending creation time. Why: Supports recent bookings for a consignee''s authorized records. How: Filter by consigneeid and order by createdon descending.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_bookings_status IS 'What: Index on booking status and descending creation time. Why: Supports review queues such as submitted bookings. How: Filter by status and order by creation time.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_journeys_booking IS 'What: Index on journey booking ID. Why: Supports loading the containers fulfilling a booking. How: Filter container_journeys by bookingid.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_journeys_eta IS 'What: Partial index on expected arrival for open journeys. Why: Supports operational ETA and overdue candidate queries. How: Filter endedon IS NULL and expectedarrival by date/time; API/report must additionally account for already-arrived shipments when calculating overdue arrivals.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_events_timeline IS 'What: Index on journey and descending occurrence/entry time. Why: Supports timeline and latest-event lookups. How: Filter by journeyid and order by occurredon then createdon.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_holds_open IS 'What: Partial index on journey ID for unreleased holds. Why: Supports current hold checks without scanning released history. How: Filter journeyid and releasedon IS NULL.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_documents_booking IS 'What: Index on document booking parent. Why: Supports loading booking attachments. How: Filter documents by bookingid and apply visibility/access checks.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_documents_journey IS 'What: Index on document journey parent. Why: Supports loading journey attachments. How: Filter documents by journeyid and apply visibility/access checks.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_documents_shipper IS 'What: Index on document shipper parent. Why: Supports loading onboarding/company attachments. How: Filter documents by shipperid and apply visibility/access checks.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_notifications_unread IS 'What: Partial index on recipient and descending creation time for unread messages. Why: Supports unread counts and recent unread notifications. How: Filter recipientid and readon IS NULL.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_tokens_user IS 'What: Index on token account owner. Why: Supports finding and revoking a user''s issued tokens. How: Filter by userid; tokenhash''s unique constraint separately supports token lookup.';
COMMENT ON INDEX kodiak.ix_audit_entity IS 'What: Index on entity name, ID and descending creation time. Why: Supports a particular record''s change history. How: Filter by entityname and entityid and order by createdon descending.';
